 const models={
  p1a2:'The picture shows four people sitting around a table in a meeting. They are talking together and looking at each other. There are papers and other work items on the table. They may be discussing a project or making a decision. I think a good meeting needs clear communication. Everyone should have a chance to speak, and the group should agree on the next actions before the meeting ends.',
  p1b2:'The picture appears to show four colleagues taking part in a small team meeting. They are seated around a table and seem actively engaged in the discussion rather than simply listening to a presentation. The papers and working materials suggest that they may be reviewing a project or trying to reach a decision. Effective group communication in this situation would depend on a clear objective, balanced participation and a concise summary of responsibilities at the end. Without those elements, even an energetic discussion can produce confusion rather than progress.',
  p2a2:'The picture shows a woman wearing a headset and working at a computer. She may be speaking to a customer on the phone. She looks focused and professional. In this kind of job, it is important to listen carefully, speak clearly and stay calm. The employee also needs to ask good questions so she can understand the customer’s problem and explain the solution.',
  p2b2:'The image shows a customer-service professional wearing a headset while working at a computer. She appears to be handling a call, possibly while checking information on screen. This type of situation requires much more than fluent speech. Active listening is essential because the employee needs to identify the real issue before proposing a solution. Clear explanations, an appropriate tone and the ability to remain calm under pressure are equally important, particularly when a customer is frustrated or the problem is complex.'
 };
