 const essayLabs=[
  {tab:'Learning',title:'People continue learning throughout life. Compare how children and adults often learn new things.',questions:['one way children may learn effectively','one way adults may learn effectively','what both groups need in order to succeed'],plan:['children: play / repetition / examples','adults: goals / experience / practical use','both: motivation + feedback + practice'],a2:'Children and adults can both learn new things, but they often learn in different ways. Children usually learn well through games, repetition and examples because they are still discovering how the world works. Adults often prefer to understand the purpose of a new skill and connect it to their experience. For example, an adult may learn a computer program faster when the training uses a real work task. However, both groups need practice, encouragement and useful feedback. In my opinion, the best learning method changes with the person, but motivation and regular practice are important at every age.',b2:'Children and adults both benefit from active learning, although the way they engage with new information often differs. Children may learn naturally through play, imitation and repeated exposure, whereas adults are more likely to connect new knowledge to previous experience and to ask how it can be applied in practice. An adult learning a digital tool, for instance, may progress faster when the training solves a real problem they already understand. Despite these differences, both groups need meaningful practice, feedback and a reason to stay motivated. Effective teaching therefore depends less on age alone than on providing relevant tasks, achievable challenges and opportunities to use what has been learned.'},
  {tab:'Technology',title:'Technology makes many everyday tasks faster, but it can also create new problems.',questions:['one important advantage','one possible disadvantage','how people can use technology more effectively'],plan:['speed / access to information','distraction / dependence / privacy','clear purpose + limits + human check'],a2:'Technology has many advantages in everyday life. It helps people communicate quickly, find information and complete tasks such as banking or booking tickets. However, it can also create problems. People may spend too much time online, become distracted or depend on technology for simple tasks. I think the best solution is to use technology with a clear purpose. For example, people can turn off unnecessary notifications and check important information before making a decision. Technology is very useful when it saves time, but it should support people rather than control their attention.',b2:'Digital technology has made everyday life significantly more efficient by giving people immediate access to information, communication and services. At the same time, convenience can create dependence, constant distraction and new concerns about privacy or accuracy. The challenge is therefore not whether technology is useful, but how deliberately it is used. People can benefit more by choosing tools that solve a specific problem, limiting unnecessary notifications and verifying important information rather than accepting every automated suggestion. In this way, technology remains a practical resource while human judgment and attention continue to guide important decisions.'},
  {tab:'Travel & culture',title:'Travel can change the way people understand other cultures.',questions:['what travelers can learn','one difficulty or risk','how to make travel more meaningful'],plan:['daily habits / language / perspectives','stereotypes / staying in tourist areas','local interaction + curiosity + respect'],a2:'Travel can help people understand other cultures because they can see daily life directly. They may learn about food, language, traditions and different ways of communicating. However, travel does not automatically create understanding. A visitor who only stays in tourist areas may keep the same stereotypes and have little contact with local people. To make travel more meaningful, I think people should be curious and respectful. They can learn a few words of the local language, visit different places and speak with local residents when possible. These experiences can help travelers compare cultures without deciding that one way is better than another.',b2:'Travel can broaden cultural understanding because it exposes people to routines, values and social conventions that are difficult to appreciate from a distance. However, simply visiting another country does not guarantee deeper awareness; travelers who remain inside familiar tourist environments may return with the same assumptions they had before. More meaningful travel requires curiosity, respectful observation and genuine interaction. Learning basic expressions in the local language, using local services and asking thoughtful questions can reveal how people experience daily life. The most valuable result is not collecting differences, but recognizing why practices make sense within a particular cultural context and reflecting on one’s own habits as well.'}
 ];
 const essayNotesKey=BASE+'GeneralEssayLabNotes',essayNotes=readJSON(essayNotesKey,{});let active=0;
 function renderGeneralEssayLab(){const item=essayLabs[active],box=$('#generalEssayLab');$$('#generalEssayTabs button').forEach((b,i)=>b.classList.toggle('active',i===active));const saved=essayNotes[active]||{};box.innerHTML=`<div class="prompt-lab-head"><span>GENERAL ESSAY SUBJECT ${active+1} / ${essayLabs.length}</span><h3>${item.title}</h3><ul>${item.questions.map(x=>`<li>${x}</li>`).join('')}</ul></div><div class="plan-workbench"><div class="plan-steps"><label>MAIN IDEA<textarea data-gen-field="main" placeholder="What is my overall answer?">${saved.main||''}</textarea></label>${item.questions.map((x,i)=>`<label>POINT ${i+1}<textarea data-gen-field="p${i}" placeholder="Idea + example / reason">${saved['p'+i]||''}</textarea></label>`).join('')}</div><div class="plan-actions"><button class="secondary" id="genPlanModel" type="button">SHOW MODEL PLAN</button><button class="secondary" data-gen-model="a2" type="button">A2–B1 ESSAY</button><button class="secondary" data-gen-model="b2" type="button">B2–C1 ESSAY</button></div><div class="plan-model hidden" id="genPlanOut"></div><div class="essay-model hidden" id="genModelOut"></div></div>`;$$('[data-gen-field]',box).forEach(el=>el.addEventListener('input',()=>{essayNotes[active]??={};essayNotes[active][el.dataset.genField]=el.value;localStorage.setItem(essayNotesKey,JSON.stringify(essayNotes));}));$('#genPlanModel').addEventListener('click',()=>{const out=$('#genPlanOut');out.classList.toggle('hidden');out.textContent=`MODEL PLAN\nOverall: answer the subject directly.\n• ${item.plan[0]}\n• ${item.plan[1]}\n• ${item.plan[2]}\nConclusion: connect the points and give a clear final view.`;});$$('[data-gen-model]',box).forEach(b=>b.addEventListener('click',()=>{const out=$('#genModelOut');out.classList.remove('hidden');out.innerHTML=`<strong>${b.dataset.genModel==='a2'?'A2–B1':'B2–C1'} MODEL</strong><br>${b.dataset.genModel==='a2'?item.a2:item.b2}`;}));}
